From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:07:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Repaint everything after the root window changes size

configure_win() dropped the back buffer and took the new root size, but
added no damage: paint_all() then created the new buffer, painted only the
damaged parts into it and copied all of it to the root, so the rest showed
whatever the new pixmap's memory held.  The whole new screen is damaged
now, and the windows' named pixmaps, pictures and shadows and the root's
background tile are dropped, so that paint_all() makes them anew: the
window manager and the desktop resize and recreate their windows around a
new screen size, and an old name kept showing the old pixmap (the desktop's
old picture at the old size).
---
 xcompmgr.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xcompmgr.c b/xcompmgr.c
index f28e4e6..70e6a6a 100644
--- a/xcompmgr.c
+++ b/xcompmgr.c
@@ -1557,6 +1557,42 @@ configure_win (Display *dpy, XConfigureEvent *ce)
 	    }
 	    root_width = ce->width;
 	    root_height = ce->height;
+	    /* the new buffer is painted only where there is damage and then
+	       copied whole to the screen: all of it is damaged, or the rest
+	       shows whatever the new pixmap's memory held.  The windows'
+	       pixmaps and pictures are named again too (the window manager
+	       and the desktop resize and recreate their windows around a
+	       new screen size; a stale name keeps showing the old pixmap),
+	       and the root's background is read again; paint_all() makes
+	       them all anew. */
+	    for (win *w2 = list; w2; w2 = w2->next)
+	    {
+#if HAS_NAME_WINDOW_PIXMAP
+		if (w2->pixmap)
+		{
+		    XFreePixmap (dpy, w2->pixmap);
+		    w2->pixmap = None;
+		}
+#endif
+		if (w2->picture)
+		{
+		    XRenderFreePicture (dpy, w2->picture);
+		    w2->picture = None;
+		}
+		if (w2->shadow)
+		{
+		    XRenderFreePicture (dpy, w2->shadow);
+		    w2->shadow = None;
+		}
+	    }
+	    if (rootTile)
+	    {
+		XRenderFreePicture (dpy, rootTile);
+		rootTile = None;
+	    }
+	    clipChanged = True;
+	    XRectangle r = { 0, 0, root_width, root_height };
+	    add_damage (dpy, XFixesCreateRegion (dpy, &r, 1));
 	}
 	return;
     }
